<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-07-29T20:15:47+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Wed, 29 Jul 2026 20:15:47 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists changed the fats in honeybees’ diets before pesticide exposure; survival rose to 90%, compared with below 50% on other diets]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132714523.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[New research suggests honey bees can better survive pesticide exposure.  Bees fed polyunsaturated fats showed a 90% survival rate.  This dietary fat type also supported nerve function and energy balance.  The findings indicate nutrition can strengthen bee resilience against agricultural stressors.  This knowledge could inform bee diets and pollinator habitat planning.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-changed-the-fats-in-honeybees-diets-before-pesticide-exposure-survival-rose-to-90-compared-with-below-50-on-other-diets/articleshow/132714523.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-changed-the-fats-in-honeybees-diets-before-pesticide-exposure-survival-rose-to-90-compared-with-below-50-on-other-diets/articleshow/132714523.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-29T19:48:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132714537,imgsize-88694.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[An Oregon EMT disabled ambulance cameras she says recorded patients without notice]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132713649.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A former EMT from Oregon has filed a lawsuit against her employer for $800,000, alleging wrongful termination after she disabled covert recording cameras present in ambulances. The company reportedly set up these cameras without informing patients or obtaining their consent. This case raises significant issues regarding patient privacy and the increasing trend of surveillance, particularly given the strict recording regulations in Oregon.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-oregon-emt-disabled-ambulance-cameras-she-says-recorded-patients-without-notice-days-later-she-was-fired-and-has-now-filed-an-800000-wrongful-termination-lawsuit/articleshow/132713649.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-oregon-emt-disabled-ambulance-cameras-she-says-recorded-patients-without-notice-days-later-she-was-fired-and-has-now-filed-an-800000-wrongful-termination-lawsuit/articleshow/132713649.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-29T19:32:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132714071,imgsize-1296754.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Meet the 13-year-old who designed affordable ‘allergy spoons']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132713730.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Abigail Stein developed an ingenious spoon designed to identify food allergens, providing a safety net for students with severe allergies during school meals. This innovative Allergy Spoon changes color upon detecting specific allergens, enhancing awareness and safety. Abigail was celebrated as a leading finalist in a prestigious young scientist challenge, with aspirations that her practical solution will address a significant concern for many families.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-abigail-stein-the-13-year-old-nashville-student-who-designed-affordable-allergy-spoons-you-dont-need-a-200-machine-to-change-the-world/articleshow/132713730.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-abigail-stein-the-13-year-old-nashville-student-who-designed-affordable-allergy-spoons-you-dont-need-a-200-machine-to-change-the-world/articleshow/132713730.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-29T19:22:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132713885,imgsize-292420.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australia built a $187,000 electric fence across Wild Horse Plain, but the real reason lies beneath one of its rarest alpine wetlands]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132713539.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A new electrified fence protects rare alpine wetlands in Kosciuszko National Park.  This enclosure safeguards endangered sphagnum bogs and associated fens from wild horse impacts.  Horse activity damages these vital peatland ecosystems and their stored carbon.  The $187,000 project was funded by biodiversity offsets from Snowy 2.0.  This targeted measure protects a small but environmentally important area within the park.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australia-built-a-187000-electric-fence-across-wild-horse-plain-but-the-real-reason-lies-beneath-one-of-its-rarest-alpine-wetlands/articleshow/132713539.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/australia-built-a-187000-electric-fence-across-wild-horse-plain-but-the-real-reason-lies-beneath-one-of-its-rarest-alpine-wetlands/articleshow/132713539.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-29T19:06:25+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132713638,imgsize-243989.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Israel elections explained: How they work, who’s in the race and what’s at stake]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132713278.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/israel-elections-explained-how-they-work-whos-in-the-race-and-whats-at-stake/articleshow/132713278.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/israel-elections-explained-how-they-work-whos-in-the-race-and-whats-at-stake/articleshow/132713278.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-29T19:32:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132714242,imgsize-62126.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[A trekking pole pierced a nurse through the torso; he then hiked 10 miles for...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132712622.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an incredible display of resilience, a nurse endured a life-threatening injury on Granite Peak in Montana. With a pole piercing his side, he bravely trekked over ten miles down the treacherous terrain. Relying on his medical expertise, he evaluated his injuries and chose to make the strenuous descent, aided by his friends. Now on the mend, he dreams of conquering the mountain again next year.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-trekking-pole-pierced-a-montana-nurse-through-the-torso-he-then-hiked-10-miles-for-six-and-a-half-hours-to-reach-help/articleshow/132712622.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-trekking-pole-pierced-a-montana-nurse-through-the-torso-he-then-hiked-10-miles-for-six-and-a-half-hours-to-reach-help/articleshow/132712622.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-29T19:04:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132713561,imgsize-1667407.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Half of England declared in drought as July records near-zero rainfall]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132711916.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/half-of-england-declared-in-drought-as-july-records-near-zero-rainfall/articleshow/132711916.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/half-of-england-declared-in-drought-as-july-records-near-zero-rainfall/articleshow/132711916.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-29T18:32:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132712996,imgsize-970563.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida sixth grader Naboshree Santra developed biodegradable soilshade balls designed to...]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132712215.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An 11-year-old Florida student has reached the finals of a national science competition.  Her innovative soilshade balls help farmers conserve water during dry weather conditions.  This eco-friendly invention slows evaporation and keeps soil moist for extended periods.  She will compete for a $25,000 prize and mentorship from 3M scientists.  The competition celebrates young innovators using STEM to solve real-world problems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/florida-sixth-grader-naboshree-santra-developed-biodegradable-soilshade-balls-designed-to-reduce-evaporation-and-retain-moisture-the-11-year-old-is-now-competing-for-a-25000-science-prize/articleshow/132712215.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/news/florida-sixth-grader-naboshree-santra-developed-biodegradable-soilshade-balls-designed-to-reduce-evaporation-and-retain-moisture-the-11-year-old-is-now-competing-for-a-25000-science-prize/articleshow/132712215.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-07-29T18:22:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-132712549,imgsize-414401.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Beneath the ocean lie 8,500 forgotten WWII shipwrecks. Many are still filled with oil]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/132711459.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![